From d3e67e9fd152ac0e66b5dbb2074f9d977e7d004c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincenzo Ceccarelli Grimaldi <vince.ceccarelli@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 10:35:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(v12): information architecture on the AWS pattern
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Restructures the whole site around six stable top-level sections, each
with an index page that never orphans its children, and makes the same
registry drive every navigation surface.

CRITICAL FIX — the site was unnavigable on mobile. Below 980 px the nav
links were set to display:none with no replacement, leaving phone
visitors a logo and one button while seven calculators, six disciplines
and four products were unreachable. There is now a real drawer with
per-section accordions, a scrim, body-scroll lock, Escape-to-close and
44 px touch targets.

- lib/nav.ts: the IA spine. Six sections (Products, Solutions, Tools,
  Capabilities, Pricing, Resources), each with index path, blurb and
  grouped items, bilingual. Header, mega-menu, drawer, footer columns,
  breadcrumbs and sitemap all derive from it, so a page in the menu is
  in the sitemap by construction.
- components/SiteHeader.tsx: desktop mega-menu with grouped items and
  blurbs; section headers are real links, so the menu enhances rather
  than gates. Skip link, aria-expanded, aria-current, focus and hover
  triggers, click-outside and Escape handling.
- components/SiteFooter.tsx: the full site index on every page.
- components/Breadcrumbs.tsx: visible trail and BreadcrumbList schema
  from one source so they cannot drift.
- components/SectionIndex.tsx: one category template, grouped exactly as
  the menu groups it.
- New: /solutions + four buyer-first solution pages, /disciplines index
  (previously orphaned), /pricing with rates stated openly, /resources.
- Mobile: single-column calculators, reduced padding, hidden brand
  subtitle, larger touch targets below 560 px.

Verified: all 68 navigation routes return 200 in both languages, the
sitemap has exactly 68 entries matching the spine, breadcrumbs render on
inner pages, and the footer index appears on every page.

